# Line endings.
#
# This repository is committed with LF and developed on Windows. Without a rule
# here, git does nothing: an editor that saves CRLF turns every file into a
# whole-file diff, and a review of ten real lines arrives as four thousand.
# That happened, which is why this file exists.
#
# text=auto eol=lf: git stores LF and checks out LF. Every tool in the
# toolchain - CMake, ninja, gcc, python, west - reads LF on Windows without
# complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except batch files. cmd.exe is the one thing here that is not indifferent to
# line endings; a .bat with bare LF can misparse labels and multi-line blocks.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.hex binary
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
